{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\IntranetAgglo\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "boot-listener",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "lib/AppInfo/Application.php:31 query()"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "boot() registers a listener or takes a service from the container in 1 place. boot() runs once for every process of the server, so each of them is built on every request. registerEventListener() in register() builds a listener only when its event fires.",
        "  lib/AppInfo/Application.php:31 query()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "route-unreferenced",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "GET /index.php/apps/intranetagglo/user  intranetagglo.page.getuserinfo  appinfo/routes.php:3 routes"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "Nothing in the app calls 1 route outside OCS. Looked for: a route name or a path in the PHP source and the templates, in 21 files of the frontend source and in the navigation of info.xml. The frontend puts the path of the app and the rest of a URL together at run time, so every text there that reads like a path below the app counted as a call. A route stays behind when the frontend stops calling it. A route that only a client outside the app calls shows here as well, unless its method allows requests from other origins (CORS).",
        "  GET /index.php/apps/intranetagglo/user  intranetagglo.page.getuserinfo  appinfo/routes.php:3 routes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ocp-deprecated",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "lib/AppInfo/Application.php:32 OCP\\Notification\\IManager::registerNotifierService(): deprecated since Nextcloud 26; use the IBootStrap registration context"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "1 use in 1 file of the public API that is deprecated in Nextcloud 20 to 30. The text of the tag names the replacement where it has one.",
        "  lib/AppInfo/Application.php:32 OCP\\Notification\\IManager::registerNotifierService(): deprecated since Nextcloud 26; use the IBootStrap registration context"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "time-direct",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "lib/Controller/NewsController.php:232 new DateTime()"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "lib/ reads the clock directly in 1 place. OCP\\AppFramework\\Utility\\ITimeFactory, a PSR-20 ClockInterface, gives the same time and can be replaced in a test.",
        "  lib/Controller/NewsController.php:232 new DateTime()"
      ]
    },
